---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/asbe/asbe26.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "1. Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "2. Scope — Reinsurance Held and Reinsurance Issued" },
        { id: "s3", label: "3. Reinsurance Contracts Held" },
        { id: "s4", label: "4. Recognition Timing — Aligned With the Underlying Contracts" },
        { id: "s5", label: "5. Reinsurance Contracts Issued (Assumed)" },
        { id: "s6", label: "6. The Same Building Block Model, Applied to Reinsurance" },
        { id: "s7", label: "7. Why a Separate Standard, Rather Than One Unified Standard" },
        { id: "s8", label: "8. Worked Example — Recognising a Reinsurance Contract Held" },
        { id: "s9", label: "9. Worked Example — Early Recognition Following an Onerous Underlying Group" },
        { id: "s10", label: "10. Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s11", label: "11. Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s12", label: "12. Relationship to IFRS 17" },
        { id: "s13", label: "13. Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s14", label: "14. Related Standards" },
        { id: "s15", label: "15. Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">
<div class="hub-sub">Extended reference poster · Chinese GAAP (ASBE / CAS) · 再保险合同 · The companion standard to ASBE No. 25, applying the same building block model to reinsurance · RMB examples</div></div></div>



<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">The companion standard applying the general model to reinsurance</div><div class="principle">ASBE No. 26 governs REINSURANCE contracts — BOTH reinsurance HELD (CEDED to ANOTHER reinsurer) and reinsurance ISSUED (ASSUMED from ANOTHER insurer) — APPLYING the SAME general BUILDING block MEASUREMENT model INTRODUCED for DIRECT insurance CONTRACTS under ASBE No. 25 (see the COMPANION poster), ADAPTED for the SPECIFIC fact PATTERNS reinsurance ARRANGEMENTS present.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope — Reinsurance Held and Reinsurance Issued</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Both sides of a reinsurance arrangement</div><div class="principle">This Standard applies to REINSURANCE contracts an INSURER HOLDS (as a CEDING company TRANSFERRING risk to a REINSURER) and REINSURANCE contracts an INSURER ISSUES (as a REINSURER ACCEPTING risk from ANOTHER insurer) — COVERING BOTH sides of the REINSURANCE relationship.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Reinsurance Contracts Held</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A separate asset, measured using the same building block principles</div><div class="text-supporting">A REINSURANCE contract HELD is RECOGNISED as a SEPARATE asset — MEASURED using FULFILMENT cash FLOWS and a CONTRACTUAL service MARGIN, PARALLELING the GENERAL model — RATHER than SIMPLY netted AGAINST the UNDERLYING direct INSURANCE liabilities it RELATES to.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Recognition Timing — Aligned With the Underlying Contracts</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Recognised no later than the underlying loss-making group</div><div class="text-supporting">A REINSURANCE contract HELD is RECOGNISED WHEN the UNDERLYING insurance CONTRACTS it RELATES to are RECOGNISED, OR — WHERE EARLIER — WHEN the UNDERLYING group of CONTRACTS becomes ONEROUS (loss-MAKING), triggering EARLIER recognition of the REINSURANCE asset'S offsetting BENEFIT.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Reinsurance Contracts Issued (Assumed)</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Measured consistently with direct insurance contracts issued</div><div class="text-supporting">WHERE an ENTERPRISE ISSUES (ASSUMES) reinsurance CONTRACTS, THEY are MEASURED CONSISTENTLY with HOW the SAME entity WOULD measure a DIRECT insurance contract ISSUED under ASBE No. 25 — the SAME building BLOCK approach, ADAPTED for the SPECIFIC terms of the REINSURANCE arrangement.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>The Same Building Block Model, Applied to Reinsurance</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Fulfilment cash flows and a contractual service margin, from the reinsurer's perspective</div><div class="text-supporting">CONSISTENT with ASBE No. 25, MEASUREMENT is BUILT from FULFILMENT cash FLOWS (probability-WEIGHTED, discounted, PLUS a risk ADJUSTMENT) and a CONTRACTUAL service MARGIN — REPRESENTING, for a REINSURANCE contract HELD, the NET COST or gain of PURCHASING reinsurance PROTECTION, recognised OVER the period REINSURANCE coverage is RECEIVED.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Why a Separate Standard, Rather Than One Unified Standard</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A structural choice, not a substantive divergence</div><div class="text-supporting">AS discussed in the COMPANION ASBE No. 25 poster, IFRS 17 addresses BOTH direct INSURANCE and REINSURANCE within a SINGLE, unified STANDARD, WHEREAS China SPLITS the EQUIVALENT guidance across TWO separate STANDARDS. This REFLECTS a GENERAL ASBE preference for SEPARATING distinct TOPIC areas into THEIR own dedicated STANDARDS, RATHER than a SUBSTANTIVE difference in the UNDERLYING measurement PRINCIPLES themselves.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — Recognising a Reinsurance Contract Held</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">A separate asset, measured on the building block basis</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Ceding a portion of catastrophe risk</div><div class="wk-body">An insurer purchases reinsurance protection for a portfolio of property policies, ceding 40% of the underlying risk. The reinsurance contract's fulfilment cash flows and CSM are measured following the general building block model.</div><div class="wk-answer">The insurer recognises a SEPARATE reinsurance CONTRACT asset, MEASURED using the SAME fulfilment CASH flow and CSM MECHANICS as its DIRECT insurance liabilities — RECOGNISED no LATER than the UNDERLYING direct policies THEMSELVES are recognised.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — Early Recognition Following an Onerous Underlying Group</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Recognising the offsetting benefit as soon as the loss is identified</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A loss-making underlying policy group triggers early recognition</div><div class="wk-body">A group of underlying direct insurance contracts becomes onerous (loss-making) before the reinsurance contract covering them would otherwise be recognised under the general timing rule.</div><div class="wk-answer">The INSURER recognises the REINSURANCE contract HELD ASSET <strong>EARLY</strong> — AT the SAME time the UNDERLYING onerous GROUP is recognised — ENSURING the OFFSETTING benefit of the REINSURANCE protection is REFLECTED WITHOUT delay.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBE No. 26 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Reconciliation of reinsurance contract assets/liabilities held and issued</span><span>Amounts recognised in profit or loss relating to reinsurance contracts</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether a group of underlying contracts is onerous, triggering early reinsurance recognition</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Probability-weighted future cash flow estimates for reinsurance arrangements</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Relationship to IFRS 17</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASBE 26 vs IFRS 17's reinsurance provisions</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASBE 26</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IFRS 17</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Measurement approach</span><span>Building block, same as direct contracts</span><span>Building block, same as direct contracts — converged</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Standard structure</span><span>Separate standard from direct contracts</span><span>Part of the same unified standard</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">MEASUREMENT principles are GENUINELY converged — the STRUCTURAL choice to SPLIT direct and REINSURANCE guidance into SEPARATE standards is the MAIN point of DIFFERENCE.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every reinsurance contract event lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Reinsurance contract held</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Recognised as a separate asset, measured on the building block basis</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 25</span><span>Direct Insurance Contracts — supplies the general building block measurement model this Standard applies to reinsurance</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Reinsurance contract held</div><div class="glossary-def">A reinsurance arrangement in which the reporting entity cedes risk to another reinsurer, recognised as a separate asset.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Onerous group</div><div class="glossary-def">A group of insurance contracts expected to be loss-making, triggering early recognition of a related reinsurance contract held.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Chinese GAAP / ASBE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (资产负债表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bp">IS</span> Income Statement (利润表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bo">SCOE</span> Statement of Changes in Owners' Equity (所有者权益变动表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bc">CFS</span> Cash Flow Statement (现金流量表)</div></div></div>


</div>
  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.asbe26 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
